  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Seat Ledger",
    "overview": "The app is stxrobotics.com carried onto a phone: a light, cool page (#f7fafc), white fields, cool hairlines, one maroon voice, and black bands that hold the numbers that matter. Its own idea is the seat ledger, a row of square ticks with one per seat. It shows up wherever a session is in play: on the camp list, in the camp detail band, in the strip above every registration step, and on the confirmation, where the parent's own seat fills maroon. The parent should always be able to see what they are holding.\n\nThe density is calm and editorial. Lists are ruled with hairlines rather than stacked as cards. Corners are square everywhere. There are no shadows. Typography is Atkinson Hyperlegible alone, using weight and size instead of a second face. One shared custom look runs on iOS and Android. It does not adapt per OS, but it keeps each OS's hard guarantees (see Layout).\n\nAnything the client has not decided is shown, not invented: it sits in a dashed blue placeholder frame that says it is a placeholder.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Square seat ticks as the core information graphic; one tick per seat.",
      "Black bands for headline numbers and context; light page for detail and forms.",
      "Maroon is the only action color; blue appears only in placeholder frames.",
      "Square corners on every surface, control and tick.",
      "Hairline-ruled lists, flat surfaces, no shadows.",
      "One family, Atkinson Hyperlegible, at 400 and 700."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Maroon is the only color that asks for action or marks ownership. In the ledger, maroon means \"yours\" and nothing else.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tuned Ground Rule",
        "body": "Ledger tones are chosen per ground. On black, use band-taken and band-muted. On light, use seat-taken and muted. Never move a light tick onto black or the reverse. Both taken tones hold at least 3:1 against their own ground.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Blue Means Undecided Rule",
        "body": "#2337ff appears only in placeholder frames. Don't use it for links or emphasis.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meta Below Rule",
        "body": "The meta line always sits directly under the heading it qualifies, never above it as a kicker or eyebrow. Test: the first text in any block is the heading.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Capped Display Rule",
        "body": "Every text style follows the OS font size up to 2x. Display is capped at 1.3x so the numeral and its ledger stay on screen.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Ground Rule",
        "body": "Separate things with a change of ground or a hairline, never with a shadow.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** show the seat ledger wherever a specific session is in play, tuned to its ground (dark tones on black, light tones on paper).",
      "**Do** give the parent's own seat maroon and nothing else in the ledger maroon.",
      "**Do** put the meta line (12 bold uppercase, 1.4 tracking) directly below the heading it qualifies.",
      "**Do** open session screens on a black band with the display numeral and ledger, then continue on the light page.",
      "**Do** pin the single solid maroon action at the bottom safe area, with outline buttons for secondary actions.",
      "**Do** rule lists with #e5e9f0 hairlines on a full-bleed white body.",
      "**Do** frame every undecided client fact in the dashed #2337ff placeholder, labelled \"Placeholder · topic\".",
      "**Do** keep targets at 44 to 52pt, honor safe areas, cap Display scaling at 1.3x, and fade instead of scaling under Reduce Motion.",
      "**Do** set the status bar per band: light over black, dark over paper."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "**Don't** round any corner.",
